## ⚙️ Setup & Installation

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/krishimhjn/task_management_API_Project.git
cd task_management_API_Project
```

### 2. Create a virtual environment

```bash
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate        # On Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
```

### 3. Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 4. Configure environment variables

Create a `.env` file in the root directory:
***You need to set up postgre Databse in you system***
```env
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://your_user:your_password@localhost:5432/your_db_name
SECRET_KEY=your_secret_key_here
ALGORITHM=HS256
```

### 5. Run database migrations

```bash
alembic upgrade head
```

### 6. Start the server

```bash
uvicorn main:app --reload
```

The API will be running at `http://localhost:8000`

---

## 📌 API Endpoints

### Auth / User

| Method | Endpoint | Description | Auth Required |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | `/user/register` | Register a new user | ❌ |
| POST | `/user/login` | Login and get JWT token | ❌ |
| GET | `/user/is_auth` | Check if token is valid | ✅ |
| GET | `/user/all_users` | Get all users | ❌ |

### Tasks

| Method | Endpoint | Description | Auth Required |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | `/tasks/create` | Create a new task | ✅ |
| GET | `/tasks/all_task` | Get all tasks for logged-in user | ✅ |
| GET | `/tasks/get_task_byid/{id}` | Get a task by ID | ✅ |
| PUT | `/tasks/update_task/{task_id}` | Update a task | ✅ |
| DELETE | `/tasks/delete_task/{task_id}` | Delete a task | ✅ |

---

## 🔐 Authentication

This API uses **Bearer Token** authentication.

1. Register a user via `POST /user/register`
2. Login via `POST /user/login` — you will receive a token
3. Pass the token in the `Authorization` header for protected routes:

```
Authorization: Bearer <your_token_here>
```

---

## 📬 Example Requests

### Register

```json
POST /user/register
{
  "name": "Krishi_Mahajan",
  "username": "krishi_mhjn",
  "password": "krishi@123",
  "email": "krishimhjn@gmail.com",
  "user_role": "user"
}
```

### Login

```json
POST /user/login
{
  "username": "Krishi_Mahajan",
  "password": "krishi@132"
}
```

### Create Task

```json
POST /tasks/create

Authorization: jwt <token>

{
  "title": "Buy groceries",
  "description": "Milk, eggs, bread",
  "is_completed": false
}




## 🌐 Deployment

My project includes a `Procfile` for deployment on platforms like **Railway** :

```
web: uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT
```

